  "source_decisions": [
    "Solana st:sol: cluster/checksum and gpst1 base58 memo exactly follow existing web formats; strict canonical prime-order/non-identity validation and KEY_REUSE rejection remain.",
    "Solana ECDH/tweak/view-tag use current web ADR0017 formulas with no cofactor multiplication because points are strictly prime order; raw-scalar signing code is unchanged.",
    "TRON st:trx:0x and GPT1 memo reuse core scheme1; old st:eth:0x is explicitly rejected.",
    "TRON build() unconditionally throws MEMO_NOT_BOUND before any derivation or randomness, since this skeleton cannot bind memo into signed bytes.",
    "CLI reports Solana cluster and rejects mainnet; legacy-address errors keep fixed value-free messages.",
    "Generator derives expected vectors from existing web implementations, not the two libraries under test; differential tests compare both implementations."
  ]
